  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Adverbios de modo** (responden a *¿cómo?*): se forman con **adjetivo + -ly**.",
      "",
      "| Adjetivo | Adverbio | Regla |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| careful | **carefully** | + -ly |",
      "| slow | **slowly** | + -ly |",
      "| happy | **happily** | y → -ily |",
      "| dangerous | **dangerously** | + -ly |",
      "| quiet | **quietly** | + -ly |",
      "",
      "**Irregulares:**",
      "",
      "- **good → well**: *She plays tennis **well**.* (no *plays good*)",
      "- **fast → fast**, **hard → hard**, **late → late**, **early → early** (igual forma)",
      "- Ojo: *hardly* significa 'apenas' (*I hardly know him*), *lately* = últimamente.",
      "",
      "**Posición:** después del verbo o del objeto: *He drives **carefully**. · She speaks English **well**.* (no *She speaks well English*).",
      "",
      "**Adjetivo vs adverbio:** *She is a careful driver.* (adj. con sustantivo) ≠ *She drives carefully.* (adv. con verbo). Con *be / look / feel / sound* se usa adjetivo: *You look happy.*",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *carefully* /ˈkeəfəli/ · *dangerously* /ˈdeɪndʒərəsli/ · *quietly* /ˈkwaɪətli/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "She speaks very good English. She sings good.",
        "right": "She speaks very good English. She sings well.",
        "note": "Después de un verbo usa well."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "He drives careful.",
        "right": "He drives carefully.",
        "note": "Para describir cómo conduce, usa el adverbio."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
